Subject: [PATCH 08/10] docs: add vxn backend guide

The vxn sandbox backend needs a vxn SDK (the `vxn` CLI) installed, which a
user builds from the meta-virtualization Yocto layer. Document the
axis-specific side: the SDK prerequisite (referring to meta-virt's
docs/vxn-sdk.md for the build), `axis run --policy vxn -- <tool>`, the env
knobs (VXN_BIN, VXN_BASE_IMAGE, VXN_FORWARD_ENV, VXN_MEMORY), how policy
network modes map to the DomU NIC, and config a vs b. Linked from the
README's Linux-backends section.

Signed-off-by: Bruce Ashfield <bruce.ashfield@gmail.com>
